Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:02.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One more limit, a proved one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.03,0:00:07.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}These two smooth random\Nsignals share one snapshot law,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.53,0:00:10.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}value and speed alike: same Rice rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.35,0:00:16.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Yet one crosses zero like a metronome,\Nthe other at uneven gaps.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.11,0:00:21.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}On three dials, Gissinger found a\Nshape in the waits between flips:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.92,0:00:27.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}a comb of short, quantized waits,\Nthen a memoryless exponential tail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.94,0:00:31.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No shoebox holds that shape;\Nit takes the movie.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.03,0:00:34.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The open question: can short runs,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.26,0:00:38.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}launched from generated states in\Nthe corridor, supply the waits?
